ML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) for hydrogen <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and its isotope, deuterium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></msub></mfenced></math>, is best described by:"}, "options": [{"id": "fc8c16", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8058"}, {"id": "e49fc6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8059"}, {"id": "a1a395", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a805a"}, {"id": "2c5a3b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a805b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a805c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b70"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52d0"], "question": {"text": "Match List - I with List - II.\n\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FokF98IjSD1sx1IDzRuutNvd3tib_-rCL8EuiBHxI3cc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "7520a9", "text": "(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a805d"}, {"id": "d4c612", "text": "(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a805e"}, {"id": "ca5eac", "text": "(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a805f"}, {"id": "aec53d", "text": "(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8060"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8061", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ea"], "question": {"text": "A process has <math><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>J</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>m</mi><mi>o</mi><msup><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>J</mi><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>m</mi><mi>o</mi><msup><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> Out of the values given below choose the minimum temperature above which the process will be spontaneous:"}, "options": [{"id": "fe74ba", "text": "<math><mn>20</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>K</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8062"}, {"id": "a2f0cf", "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><mi>K</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8063"}, {"id": "3bb5f6", "text": "<math><mn>12</mn><mi>K</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8064"}, {"id": "912ae9", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi>K</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8065"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8066", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4725"], "question": {"text": "<p>What happens when methane undergoes combustion in systems A and B respectively?</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F90d0d61e-7a3b-4fc2-bdd5-aad76875eb6f.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 406px; height: 121px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7d9eac", "text": "<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>System A</td>\t\t\t<td>System B</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Temperature rises</td>\t\t\t<td>Temperature remains same</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8067"}, {"id": "d1b555", "text": "<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>System A</td>\t\t\t<td>System B</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Temperature remains same</td>\t\t\t<td>Temperature rises</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8068"}, {"id": "74cf90", "text": "<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>System A</td>\t\t\t<td>System B</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Temperature falls</td>\t\t\t<td>Temperature remains same</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8069"}, {"id": "bba863", "text": "<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>System A</td>\t\t\t<td>System B</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Temperature falls</td>\t\t\t<td>Temperature rises</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a806a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a806b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b70"], "concepts": ["6176f3eb6581241c7072a3e6"], "question": {"text": "<p>For a reaction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>nO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>The free energy change is plotted as a function of temperature. The temperature below which the oxide is stable could be inferred from the plot as the point at which :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "6eda1e", "text": "the slope change from negative to positive", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a806c"}, {"id": "b5262f", "text": "the free energy change show a change from negative to positive value", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a806d"}, {"id": "eef6d6", "text": "the slope changes from positive to negative", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a806e"}, {"id": "9e91ef", "text": "the slope changes from positive to zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a806f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8070", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb8"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>CO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math></p><p>When coal of purity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> is allowed to burn in presence of insufficient oxygen, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of carbon is converted into &#39; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi></math>&#39; and the remaining is converted into &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&#39;.</p><p>The heat generated when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> of coal is burnt is</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c9bcbc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8071"}, {"id": "aac7e3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8072"}, {"id": "92271b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8073"}, {"id": "bf28a1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8074"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8075", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["61adb6e7dec0c790740ad921"], "question": {"text": "The standard reaction Gibbs energy for a chemical reaction at an absolute temperature $\\mathrm{T}$ is given by $\\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}=\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{BT}$ where A and $B$ are non-zero constants. Which of the following is true about this reaction?"}, "options": [{"id": "1f0737", "text": "Exothermic if $B  < 0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8076"}, {"id": "c89fe1", "text": "Endothermic if $\\mathrm{A}>0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8077"}, {"id": "d61d3d", "text": "Endothermic if $\\mathrm{A}  < 0$ and $\\mathrm{B}>0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8078"}, {"id": "fcbe5c", "text": "Exothermic if $\\mathrm{A}>0$ and $\\mathrm{B}  < 0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8079"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a807a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["61adb568dec0c790740ac549"], "question": {"text": "The effect of temperature on spontaneity of reactions are represented as :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F1ZEquUl0SRyTdOqwYtc03QXApfIIP5nB5RkWupFcWV8.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>"}, "options": [{"id": "7d8306", "text": "(B) and (C) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a807b"}, {"id": "001e63", "text": "(B) and (D) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a807c"}, {"id": "34da87", "text": "(A) and (D) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a807d"}, {"id": "32c0a4", "text": "(A) and (C) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a807e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a807f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e57"], "question": {"text": "Which one of the following equations does not correctly represent the first law of thermodynamics for the given processes involving an ideal gas? (Assume non- expansion work is zero)"}, "options": [{"id": "c7d5ea", "text": "Isochoric process : <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8080"}, {"id": "e21f1c", "text": "Isochoric process : <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8081"}, {"id": "ac0a22", "text": "Cyclic process : <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8082"}, {"id": "527686", "text": "Adiabatic process : <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8083"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f9b2ee0e063d92a8084", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b61"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following graphs correctly represents the variation of thermodynamic properties of Haber's process?"}, "options": [{"id": "7d6611", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FOhIfyybNykd8rAxfxdZvsjmoSoJs6iFdcYXtX2rXtdI.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69d